{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082417-matter-sphere-question","id":1082417,"title":"Matter Sphere question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-22T15:58:13-07:00","id":1082417,"title":"Matter Sphere question","content":"I'm a little fuzzy on the rules. What's the minimum sphere level to create swords, then guns? Then I need prime 2 to make them permanent? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2526-aazen","name":"Aazen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:05:26-07:00","id":1082419,"title":"","content":"Swords and things without moving parts would be Mater 3. Mater 4 will make you guns. Prime 2 won't make them permament but will allow you to make them out of thin air. <br /> <br /> 10 successes over what is needed for the effect can make them permanent if your ST agrees but they could still be dispelled / countermagicked. Mater 5 will make them permanent objects of creation unaffected by such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:47:41-07:00","id":1082435,"title":"","content":"I think the general rule is Matter 2 &gt; homogonous substances, Matter 3 &gt; complex objects of multiple substances, Matter 4 &gt; machines, and Matter 5 &gt; otherwise impossible substances or ones with unique sets of properties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082417-matter-sphere-question?p=1082419#post1082419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swords and things without moving parts would be Mater 3. Mater 4 will make you guns. Prime 2 won't make them permament but will allow you to make them out of thin air.<br /> <br /> 10 successes over what is needed for the effect can make them permanent if your ST agrees but they could still be dispelled / countermagicked. Mater 5 will make them permanent objects of creation unaffected by such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some house rules make it so you could also spend a point of Quintessence to make the creation permanent. Up to Storyteller decision, but I find more options to be a good thing, everything else being equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}